{
  "$comment": "The frozen recipe of the P7 synthetic STT corpus (build_corpus.py). Changing anything here changes recipe_sha256 and so the corpus identity in every report and score: bump `name` when you do. Speech is brought to an active level of -26 dBFS +- 4 dB (seeded per utterance, the same under every condition). SNRs are active-level ratios (see corpus/dsp.py: mean power of the 20 ms frames within 30 dB of the 95th-percentile frame). FLEURS (CC-BY-4.0) gives the speech; FMA commercial-use tracks (one 16 kHz shard) the music; ESC-50 (CC BY-NC 3.0) the effects.",
